WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Your tag is probably the
most important element.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.934
I look for one high-visibility
spot, and I put my name up.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.430
50-something years of
working with this medium.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.960
I've lived many lives.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.100
Grew up as "Lenny."

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.670
Recently became "Leonard, Futura,
Futura 2000, Futura Dos Mil."

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.469
But I will answer
to "Yo", no problem.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:30.270
I'm part of a school of art and
a culture that invented itself.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.310
The movement left a legacy.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.440
Things that were
emerging in the 80s

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.950
were beginning to open our
eyes up beyond the subway.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:42.400
To me, the abstraction always
appeared inside the letters,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.280
and what I was saying is, like,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.540
"Wow, what if you took the letter away?"

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.710
So in this class, I'm
going to teach you

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.750
how to use spray paint.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.980
I would say that can
is sufficiently shaken.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.470
How to paint this line,
the thickness of that.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.780
Spraying upside down,
that's essentially

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.612
how I'm able to control
the width of my lines.

00:01:07.612 --> 00:01:09.820
I'm going to walk through
the creation of a painting,

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.840
and I'm also going to talk
about my world of abstraction,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.101
and how that might apply
for you and your work.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.460
Find your own techniques.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.459
I'm going to try to follow
that line, and there you go.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.410
1970, my mom came
to me with a story:

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.167
"We're not your
biological family."

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.400
I got an identity crisis.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.220
It's the age-old
question, "Who am I?"

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.840
The graffiti thing that was
happening outside my door

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.950
seemingly was an answer.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.920
I could hide under the
anonymous pseudonym

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.574
of this new character.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.300
That's the impetus for me
becoming the graffiti writer

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.710
that I became.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.470
Don't be deterred by what
may or may not be a mistake.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.670
If I were suddenly like,
"Oh, no, what did I do?"

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.830
Hey, it's no problem.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.760
Canvases can be repainted white.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.637
Do something you think
you can't do,

00:01:59.637 --> 00:02:00.970
and you might surprise yourself.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.170
I just invented that.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.460
I never did that before.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.896
If someone like me found my
way, you should have no problem.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.860
You don't even need a canvas
to paint or a wall to tag.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.404
All you need is an idea
and a can of spray paint.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.931
I'm Futura, and this
is my MasterClass.

